    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1913 Rancho Bernardo Schoolhouse now houses the town’s Historical Museum, preserving artifacts and stories for future generations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/2632"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1982, local citizens founded the Rancho Bernardo Historical Society to safeguard the community’s heritage amid rapid change.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/2632"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The museum’s collection features photographs, documents, and living‑history reenactments that bring Rancho Bernardo’s past to life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/2632"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rancho Bernardo’s terrain of canyons, rolling hills, and bedrock outcroppings shapes its Mediterranean climate with dry summers and mild winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rancho_Bernardo%2C_San_Diego"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The community’s name originates from the 1842‑1845 Rancho San Bernardo Mexican land grant, linking it to California’s early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
